  Pairwise, tau = 0.54 puts ZERO of the 621 adjudicated 'different' pairs above the line. Closing the merge relation transitively puts 19 of them into one card anyway (3.06%) and grows a runaway cluster of 575 notices: similarity is not transitive and single linkage does not care. Anchoring every member to the card's canonical notice cuts that to 1 (0.161%) but still allows a star of radius tau, which is where the last one comes from. Requiring the new notice to clear tau against EVERY existing member takes false merges to 0 and caps the largest card at 9. The price is recall: 190 of 279 adjudicated duplicates end up on one card, against 194 under single linkage. Under a 50:1 ratio that is the trade the ratio exists to make.

